<title>SWITZERLAND: Swiss Crea think tank sees 0.7 pct 1997 gdp growth.</title>
<headline>Swiss Crea think tank sees 0.7 pct 1997 gdp growth.</headline>
<dateline>LAUSANNE, Switzerland 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The University of Lausanne's Crea economic research institute kept its forecast for Swiss economic growth at 0.7 percent in 1997.</p>
<p> (in pct/1996 figs actual) 1996    1997   1998   1999</p>
<p> GDP			     -0.7    +0.7   +1.2   +2.0</p>
<p> Household consumption     +0.3    +0.8   +1.4   +1.4</p>
<p> Fixed investment	    +1.3    +1.5   +0.8   +1.2</p>
<p>    plant			-3.5    -1.7   -0.6   +0.3</p>
<p>    equipment		  +8.4    +5.9   +2.6   +2.3</p>
<p> Exports of goods, svcs    +2.4    +2.5   +4.0   +4.5</p>
<p> Imports of goods, svcs    +1.5    +3.4   +3.9   +3.0</p>
<p> SNB Swiss franc index     -1.8    -7.8   +0.8   +2.5</p>
<p> Average real salaries     +0.5    -0.1   +0.7   +0.4</p>
<p>Inflation</p>
<p>    CPI			  +0.8    +1.0   +1.1   +1.7</p>
<p>    GDP deflator	     +0.1    +0.3   +0.9   +1.9</p>
<p>Average interest rates</p>
<p>    three-month deposits    1.4     2.1    2.2    2.3</p>
<p>    govt bond yields	  4.0     3.3    3.1    3.1</p>
<p> Average unemployment rate  4.7     5.5    5.3    5.3</p>
<p>Current account surplus</p>
<p>  (billions of Sfr)	  25.3    17.5   15.8   18.8</p>
<p>-- Zurich newsroom +41 1 631 7340</p>
</text>
